yze a saved log bundle instead of a live model\n./juju_errors_to_slack.py --input debuglog.txt -w $WEBHOOK\n```\n\nNotes:\n- Webhook URL can come from `JUJU_ERRORS_WEBHOOK_URL`; channel override via `--channel`/`JUJU_ERRORS_SLACK_CHANNEL`.\n- Only stdlib (`urllib`, `subprocess`) — no dependencies.\n- If you'd rather target a channel via Slack API instead of a webhook, you'd swap `post_to_slack` to use `chat.postMessage` with a bot token — happy to add that variant if useful.","n_tool_calls":3,"usage":{"input":7989,"output":3296,"cost":0.0,"cacheRead":5056,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":178,"totalTokens":16341},"dur_s":63}
